# What NOT to ship to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# Dockerfile.cuvslam-foxy copies exactly one file (docker/entrypoint_foxy.sh); everything
# else this project needs - the repo, third_party/cuVSLAM, the calibration - is BIND-MOUNTED
# at runtime by docker-compose.yml. So the build context should be tiny, and without this
# file it is not: on the board it was 935 MB, and `docker compose build` spent minutes
# streaming recordings and a git history to the daemon before running Step 1 of 26.
#
# This lived only on the board until 2026-09-02, and had been disabled there (renamed to
# .dockerignore.tx2bak), so nothing was excluded at all. Tracked here so it applies wherever
# the image is built.
.git
third_party

# build outputs - regenerated by `docker compose run --rm build-ws`
build
install
log

# recordings and datasets: bags/vo_input alone was 524 MB
bags
datasets
*.log
*.pdf
scripts/config
